<!--
  Detection : Scheduled Task Persistence (schtasks.exe)
  Lab       : soc-home-lab (Wazuh 4.9.2, Win10 Target + Sysmon)
  Install   : /var/ossec/etc/rules/local_rules.xml
              then: systemctl restart wazuh-manager
  Rule ID   : 100003 (custom range 100000+)

  Description:
    100003  Fires when a Sysmon process-creation event (Event ID 1,
            matched via built-in rule 61603) has an originalFileName of
            schtasks.exe — i.e., the Windows Task Scheduler command-line
            tool was used to create, modify, or run a scheduled task.
            Level 12.

  MITRE ATT&CK:
    T1053.005  Scheduled Task/Job: Scheduled Task

  Validated against a real run:
    - Command executed manually on the target (not via Kali — this
      scenario, like the PowerShell one, simulates post-exploitation
      activity by running the command directly on Target-host):
        schtasks /create /tn "ScheduledTaskDemo" /tr "calc.exe" /sc onlogon /f
    - This creates a task that launches calc.exe at the next interactive
      logon. calc.exe is a harmless stand-in for a real payload in this
      lab; /f forces creation without a confirmation prompt.
    - Unlike the RDP and PowerShell scenarios, this command succeeded —
      the task was actually created ("УСПЕХ. Запланированная задача
      ... была успешно создана").
    - Sysmon Event 1 recorded the process creation with the full command
      line, parent process (powershell.exe), and user context
      (DESKTOP-478GG5N\Target-host).
    - Rule 100003 fired 3 times during testing (firedtimes: 3) — see the
      investigation's Lessons Learned for context.

  Investigation: ../investigations/scheduled-task-persistence.md

  Future work:
    - Add a complementary rule watching the Microsoft-Windows-TaskScheduler
      operational log directly (Event ID 106 "task registered"), to cross-
      check findings against the Sysmon-based detection here.
    - Extend the field match beyond originalFileName to also catch
      schtasks.exe invoked via a renamed binary or full path variations.
-->
<group name="windows,persistence,">

  <rule id="100003" level="12">
    <if_sid>61603</if_sid>
    <field name="win.eventdata.originalFileName">schtasks.exe</field>
    <description>Custom: Scheduled Task Creation Detected (MITRE T1053.005)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1053.005</id>
    </mitre>
  </rule>

</group>
